4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"cda685c88fcfb81661cfaff79bc3de7a7625299f2b5655e00fba490afc89e0ab","event_uuid":"5fffc92b-e74b-40bb-9a74-a460c77b5b9b","position":{"commit_sha":"334c98c06d8c9974a4c37b3e1f436b69ad695856","position":"1788908503310009001-5fffc92b-e74b-40bb-9a74-a460c77b5b9b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0934f4e5c9633d13e6846d97528dabdb7f431ac2a8d23d8ec53c01171536f938","event_uuid":"ecd47c43-5533-47c6-8035-6e285b049f5f","position":{"commit_sha":"c91938edf0895f85e9cf24093ac43ab80642e3a5","position":"1788908566916685001-ecd47c43-5533-47c6-8035-6e285b049f5f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3843676cb7a052cecd2f3154c00768338c9a14b6512c53f592b2daaedeace7c4","event_uuid":"f7c45d22-3dcc-4418-97f1-1722426264fd","position":{"commit_sha":"c91938edf0895f85e9cf24093ac43ab80642e3a5","position":"1788908577080349001-f7c45d22-3dcc-4418-97f1-1722426264fd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-263_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"be769312-72b1-4fcd-9c80-8acb1d51d151","comments":[],"created_at":1788906619370385001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Problem\n\n`docs/experiments/calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py` cannot produce a trustworthy replay.\nCORRECTION (E) in `docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md` records that it reads\nno routing index, so every re-run reproduces two known-wrong rows — `sec` reported as a\nDET/attestation gate (it is an LLM synonym of `security`) and `project.review-phase-boundaries`\nreported at the 0.95 unknown-criterion default rather than the 0.90 the project overlay sets.\nFixing it was deferred there.\n\nSeparately, `IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION` moved to **code-v5** on 2026-08-21\n(`src/rebar/llm/code_review/sidecar.py:35`), while the script's `--impact-model-version` still\ndefaults to a hardcoded `code-v3`. ADR 0036 forbids pooling across versions, so the default\nsilently analyses a retired cohort. No code-v5 calibration record exists in-tree.\n\n## Scope\n\n1. `docs/experiments/calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py` — read routing and label synonyms\n   through the production path (`registry.effective_routing`, `registry.normalize_criteria`)\n   with a pure-JSON fallback for checkouts where `rebar` is not importable; identify DET\n   criteria by their routing `exec` rather than a validity heuristic; default\n   `--impact-model-version` to the version the gate stamps today; print each proposal as a\n   DELTA against committed routing, showing UNROUTED distinctly from a deliberate advisory;\n   add `--dump-newly-blocking CRIT=THR`, which writes the findings a proposed flip would ADD\n   (priority in `[THR, current_threshold)`) to JSON for content adjudication.\n2. `docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md` — mark CORRECTION (E) resolved,\n   describing what changed and the verification below.\n3. `docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration-code-v5.md` — NEW. The calibration-4\n   record over the code-v5 segment: corpus and method, the per-flip adjudication, the severity\n   floor measured and rejected, the zero-impact analysis, the friction table, and corpus\n   hygiene. This is the artifact a later routing change cites.\n\n   **Segment size, measured before writing:** the code-v5 segment at\n   `<checkout>/.tickets-tracker` holds **1,135 sidecars / 703 changes / 3,573 pooled findings**\n   (2026-08-21 -> 2026-09-08), with a skipped remainder of 7,757 sidecars\n   (different_version=2,153, wrong_schema=5,604). That is two orders of magnitude above the\n   script's `MIN_N = 25` per-criterion power floor, so a per-flip adjudication is supportable.\n   The two criteria the record adjudicates carry n=55 (`security`) and n=68 (`concurrency`)\n   within the segment.\n\n   **Fallback if the segment is thin:** a criterion whose in-segment n is below `MIN_N = 25`\n   is recorded as LOW-DATA with its measured n and NO proposal — the record states the\n   insufficiency rather than presenting an underpowered adjudication, and any flip resting on\n   it is deferred. This mirrors the script's own LOW-DATA class and the code-v4 precedent,\n   where `concurrency` was held at n=1 for exactly this reason.\n\nThis ticket changes NO gate behaviour: it touches only `docs/experiments/`.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nAny edit to `src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json` or to the tests that pin it.\nApplying the flips this record clears is sibling work that depends on this ticket.\n\n## Back-out\n\nRevert the three files; nothing else reads them at runtime.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The generator is routing-aware: on the code-v3 segment it emits no `sec` row and no\n      `documentation` row (both normalize into `security` / `docs`).\n      Oracle: `python docs/experiments/calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py --tracker <checkout>/.tickets-tracker --impact-model-version code-v3`\n      produces no output line whose first field is `sec` or `documentation`.\n- [ ] The same run reports `project.review-phase-boundaries` at its overlay threshold.\n      Oracle: that run's `project.review-phase-boundaries` row shows `adv@0.90`, not 0.95.\n- [ ] The version default tracks the gate rather than a literal, verified by BEHAVIOUR not by\n      grepping the source (a substring check passes falsely on a reformat).\n      Oracle: a bare run (no `--impact-model-version`) prints\n      `[segmented to impact_model_version=code-v5]`, matching\n      `python -c \"from rebar.llm.code_review.sidecar import IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION as v;print(v)\"`.\n- [ ] `--dump-newly-blocking` writes the additive set.\n      Oracle: `python docs/experiments/calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py --tracker <checkout>/.tickets-tracker --dump-newly-blocking security=0.45 --dump-to /tmp/$$-nb.json`\n      exits 0 and the JSON key `security@0.45` holds only findings whose `priority` is\n      >= 0.45 and < 0.54.\n- [ ] CORRECTION (E) is marked resolved.\n      Oracle: `grep -c \"CORRECTION (E) — RESOLVED\" docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md`\n      returns 1.\n- [ ] The pure-JSON fallback path agrees with the production path it stands in for.\n      Oracle: a run with `rebar` importable and a run with it unavailable produce the same\n      per-criterion `now` column (postures and thresholds) on the same segment.\n- [ ] The code-v5 record exists and states its corpus size and method.\n      Oracle: `test -f docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration-code-v5.md` exits 0 and\n      the file contains the corpus line and a per-flip adjudication table.\n- [ ] `make verify` is green.\n- [ ] The Gerrit change is MERGED (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/experiments/calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py","reason":"routing-aware via effective_routing + normalize_criteria; DET by exec; dynamic version default; delta proposals; --dump-newly-blocking"},{"path":"docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration-code-v5.md","reason":"NEW: the calibration-4 record over the code-v5 segment"},{"path":"docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md","reason":"mark CORRECTION (E) resolved"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"ecd47c43-5533-47c6-8035-6e285b049f5f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["calibration","code-review"],"ticket_id":"2629-03a8-f93b-4457","ticket_type":"task","title":"Make the code-review calibration generator routing-aware and land the code-v5 record","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b598a4fe-5da5-48ae-996c-ff91e3d7ed44","73ed9e46-f38b-4c50-8892-f1970b2c1ae3","b456960e-3135-4ca2-944a-242adc2f8ee4","5fffc92b-e74b-40bb-9a74-a460c77b5b9b","ecd47c43-5533-47c6-8035-6e285b049f5f","f7c45d22-3dcc-4418-97f1-1722426264fd"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788912469581462001,"uuid":"8fbd8ff7-c1f3-453b-8a80-dbb607c867f7"}